# Listing photographs fetched by phase0/harvest_listing_images.py.
#
# THESE MUST NOT BE COMMITTED, and the reason is not disk space.
#
# They are third parties' copyrighted photographs, published by us under a
# stated promise: credited, linked, and REMOVED ON REQUEST. Git history is
# permanent. Commit them and `--optout` deletes the working file while every
# copy stays recoverable in the repo forever — which turns the promise on
# every listing page into something we cannot actually keep, and makes the
# removal we told an agency we performed a thing we did not perform.
#
# A takedown has to remove the file. That rules out version control.
#
# Regenerable in ~46 minutes:  python3 harvest_listing_images.py
# They are disposable in the §3 sense — cache/, *.sqlite — not precious in
# the id_anchors.json sense. Nothing here was measured by a human.
assets/listing/

# Build output. Rebuilt by build.py, which installs only after all gates
# pass; dist-site/ carries its own .gitignore for the Vercel link.
dist-index/
dist-contradictions/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
